# Testing conventions — {{PROJECT_NAME}}

<!-- Loaded only when working with files matching the paths above. Edit globs to match
     this project (e.g. "tests/**/*", "**/*.test.ts", "**/*_test.py"). -->

- Run the suite with `{{TEST_CMD}}`; it must pass before a task is marked done.
- Tests must be able to **fail** when behavior is wrong — no tautological assertions.
- Cover the failure modes, not just the happy path: invalid input, boundaries, empty/null, errors.
- Keep tests deterministic (no hidden time/order/network dependence).
- Test behavior and contracts, not volatile implementation details.
